Elkulator patch 04: working fullscreen on modern X servers
Fullscreen asked for an 800x600 video mode via XF86VidMode, which the
Raspberry Pi KMS/modesetting X driver cannot provide, so the picture sat
unscaled in the corner of the screen. Fullscreen is now a borderless
window the size of the desktop (no video mode switch, so it also works
when the launcher halves the resolution with xrandr --scale), and the
640x512 picture is scaled to fit:
  elk.cfg  fullscreen_scale = 0  largest whole-number scale (default, sharp)
                              1  4:3 aspect
                              2  fill the screen
  elk.cfg  display_scale = 2     read by the RetroPie launcher:
                                 2 = X at half the TV resolution, doubled
                                     by the display (menus twice the size)
                                 1 = X at the full TV resolution
                                 (Elkulator itself only keeps the value)
Adds the -fullscreen command line option to start in fullscreen.

